{
  "description": "Cross-engine record for the pattern form of spec 10.7.4. Each case: a pattern, a value, whether the pattern has the restricted I-Regexp form (`form`, checked by scripts/check.ts), and whether the value matches in ECMAScript with the u flag and in the Rust regex crate (true, false, or \"error\" when the engine refuses the pattern). scripts/check.ts verifies `form` and `ecmascript`, scripts/regex-parity verifies `rust`. For every case of the form that both engines compile the two must agree, unless the case carries `difference` of kind `unicode-version`: one code point whose general category differs between the two engines' Unicode tables, which each engine verifies on its own side. Every pattern a valid example uses is listed here.",
